.TH std::sortable 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::sortable \- std::sortable

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <iterator>
template< class I, class Comp = ranges::less, class Proj = std::identity >

concept sortable =                                                          \fI(since C++20)\fP
std::permutable<I> &&

std::indirect_strict_weak_order<Comp, std::projected<I, Proj>>;

The sortable concept specifies the requirements for algorithms that permute a range into
an ordered range according to Comp.

  Semantic requirements

std::sortable<I, Comp, Proj> is modeled only if all concepts it subsumes are modeled.

